      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Toronto Maple Leafs didn't just shuffle the offseason deck - they flipped the table, betting big on a Hall of Fame goaltender to resurrect a franchise that finished 8th in the Atlantic with 78 points and missed the playoffs. <strong>Sergei Bobrovsky agrees to a three-year, $21M deal with the Maple Leafs</strong>, reuniting with the 2024 Stanley Cup-winning tandem and shielding the team from Anthony Stolarz's injury history. General Manager John Chayka, nowhere to be found on a dock, crushed two trades and five signings before Canada Day even ignited, including Nick Paul, Jack Roslovic, and depth forwards to flesh out the roster. At 37, Bobrovsky brings a career-churned resume but a proven edge in high-stakes games - exactly what this cap-tight team needs. <strong>What to watch for now: how quickly Bobrovsky locks in during camp and whether the Leafs can finally stabilize their crease for a playoff push next season.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 2, 2026"
      },
