      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Blue Jays finally cracked the code, turning a packed Rogers Centre into a stress-free Canada Day celebration with <strong>a 9-3 rout of the Mets</strong>. Rookie Sean Keys, the story of the night, flipped the game wide open with his first major league home run - a three-run blast that broke the 2-0 tie and gave the team a lead they've rarely felt this season. Sitting at 41-46 and third in the AL East, 11 games behind the division lead, the Jays are fighting for a Wild Card spot, but this win offers a blueprint: contact, power, and bullpen dominance, as Spencer Miles delivered three scoreless innings. Keys' emergence is the spark they need, but the road remains steep. <strong>Next up, a Saturday night showdown at Seattle against the Mariners at 9:10 PM ET</strong>, where the Blue Jays must prove this isn't just a holiday fluke.",
