        "body": "The Toronto Raptors have abandoned the slow rebuild for a high-stakes gamble, trading their future to resurrect a champion. <strong>Superstar Kawhi Leonard is officially returning to Toronto</strong> in a blockbuster deal that sends Brandon Ingram, Gradey Dick, and two unprotected first-round picks to the Clippers, while Leonard signs a two-year, $126 million extension. After a season that ended with a 46-36 record and a third-place finish in the Atlantic Division, the front office has bet everything on the 35-year-old's final year to ignite a title run. The loss of young talent like Dick and Ingram leaves a void, but the arrival of Leonard shifts the entire narrative from patience to urgency. <strong>What to watch now is whether Leonard's legacy can override the cost of the team's future</strong> as camp opens and the new roster faces its first real test.",
